README for RudeSocket
See the end of file for copying conditions


*** INTRODUCTION ***

RudeSocket is a library that provides client socket services to an
application.  In addition to normal TCP connections, it supports TLS, proxies,
SOCKS4 and SOCKS5 servers, and chaining proxies together.

Full documentation, including a quick start and API notes, is in README.md.


*** BUILDING ***

RudeSocket builds with CMake:

	cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
	cmake --build build
	ctest --test-dir build
	cmake --install build

Then include <rude/socket.h> and link with -lrudesocket, or use
find_package(rudesocket) from CMake, or pkg-config.

TLS support requires OpenSSL and is enabled automatically when it is found.
Build with -DRUDESOCKET_WITH_SSL=OFF to leave it out.  Note that when
linking the static library, pkg-config needs --static to pull in
-lssl and -lcrypto.

The autotools build (configure / Makefile.am) was removed in this release.
It had been deprecated since the CMake build landed, and its shipped
config.guess dated from 2003, so it could not configure on any ARM machine -
which today means every Apple Silicon Mac and every ARM Linux server.  If you
need it, check out the v1.4.1 tag or earlier.

